  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An ideal gas in a thermally insulated vessel at internal pressure = <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> , volume = <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and absolute temperature = <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> expands irreversibly against zero external pressure, as shown in the diagram. The final internal pressure, volume and absolute temperature of the gas are <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , respectively. For this expansion,<br ><br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/image2-1ac2a0f3-ab7f-4534-9566-f76b23fbae75.jpg\"/></p>",
    "image": null
  },
